Package: snipflow
Version: @VERSION@
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: SnipFlow <https://github.com/YuLiangLin/SnipFlow>
Homepage: https://github.com/YuLiangLin/SnipFlow
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35), libgcc-s1, libstdc++6, zlib1g, libicu74 | libicu72 | libicu70, libssl3 | libssl3t64, libx11-6, libxrandr2, libxi6, libxcursor1, libice6, libsm6, libfontconfig1, xdg-utils
Recommends: ffmpeg, libvlc5, vlc-plugin-base, tesseract-ocr, tesseract-ocr-eng, tesseract-ocr-chi-tra, tesseract-ocr-chi-sim, xdg-desktop-portal, xdg-desktop-portal-gnome | xdg-desktop-portal-kde | xdg-desktop-portal-gtk, gstreamer1.0-pipewire, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, libgstreamer1.0-0, libgstreamer-plugins-base1.0-0, fonts-noto-cjk
Suggests: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Description: Screenshots, annotations, scrolling capture and screen recording
 SnipFlow captures regions, windows and screens, annotates them with arrows,
 shapes, text and mosaic, stitches scrolling pages, recognizes text locally,
 records the screen to MP4 and edits recordings with text and image overlays.
 Works in GNOME, KDE and other desktops on X11 and Wayland (through
 xdg-desktop-portal).
